# {{ instruction_filename }}

This file gives {{ host_name }} contributor guidance for the `claude-kit` repository. The package
produces native Claude Code and Codex configurations from one provider-neutral source. Never make a
host port by mechanically renaming paths, tools, models, or commands.

## Repository purpose

`claude-kit` is an evidence-gated, stack-agnostic SDLC configuration package. It ships no
application code or mandatory container setup. Backward-compatible public names remain:

- PyPI package: `claude-code-kit`
- Python module: `claude_kit`
- CLI executables: `ckit` (preferred), `claude-kit`, and `claude-sdlc`

The provider-neutral installation flow is:

```text
Selection
    -> catalog.resolve()
    -> ResolvedPlan
    -> ProjectionCompiler
        -> ClaudeRenderer
        -> CodexRenderer
    -> staged validation
    -> transactional installation
```

Runtime is an installation concern represented by `InstallRequest`. Do not add it to `Selection`
or branch on it inside `catalog.resolve()`. A dual-runtime install resolves once and renders twice.

Every fresh runtime-aware install has one mutable control plane under `.ckit/`: one manifest,
transaction journal, continuity file, memory store, pipeline snapshot, and evidence ledger. Legacy
Claude installs under `.claude/` remain readable and migrate transactionally. Never create a
provider-local second ledger.

## Native output surfaces

```text
Claude
  CLAUDE.md
  .claude/{agents,skills,rules,hooks,templates,scripts}/
  .claude/settings.json
  .mcp.json

Codex
  AGENTS.md
  .agents/skills/
  .codex/agents/*.toml
  .codex/hooks.json
  .codex/hooks/
  .codex/config.toml

Shared
  .ckit/
```

Codex uses lowercase `.codex`, repository skills in `.agents/skills`, custom agents in
`.codex/agents`, and a generated plugin package rooted at `providers/codex/claude-kit` (with its
manifest at `providers/codex/claude-kit/.codex-plugin/plugin.json`). The untracked local
`.codex/` directory that may exist in this checkout is developer state, not distributable input.
Preserve unique local content and never package it.

The pip scaffolder is the first-class project projection path. Static plugins expose only the
subset their hosts discover; plugin installation does not select a stack/profile/scope, create
`.ckit`, or project project-specific agents and instructions. Keep that distinction explicit.

## Source of truth and generated compatibility surfaces

Provider-neutral definitions live under `canonical/`, semantic catalog data under `catalog/`, and
provider adapters under `src/claude_kit/`. The root Claude plugin payload and provider manifests are
generated compatibility surfaces. Do not hand-edit generated output.

Important generators:

```bash
python scripts/gen_provider_payloads.py
python scripts/gen_provider_payloads.py --check
python scripts/gen_provider_manifests.py
python scripts/gen_provider_manifests.py --check
python scripts/gen_hooks.py
python scripts/gen_hooks.py --check
python scripts/gen_contributor_guides.py
python scripts/gen_contributor_guides.py --check
```

Canonical agent, skill, rule, command, hook, workflow, template, and MCP definitions must use
semantic capabilities and symbolic references such as `agent://`, `skill://`, `rule://`, and
`state://`. They must not contain provider tool names, provider model aliases, permission syntax,
or physical host paths. Renderers are the only layer that resolves those semantics.

